"\n\"United States\",341784857\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912510976},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see:\n1. The farmers markets data includes state names and the number of farmers markets per state\n2. The census data has the 2025 U.S. population: 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check what the full farmers markets data looks like to understand if there are territories I need to exclude\n2. Sum the farmers_markets column (excluding territories)\n3. Create a metric for farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nLet me peek at all the state names in the farmers markets data to see if there are territories listed.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01XvdsgtSLHo33iTGTeiBc83","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.select('state_name')","limit":0}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":257,"cacheRead":16915,"cacheWrite":774,"totalTokens":17960,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0012850000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0016915,"cacheWrite":0.0009675,"total":0.003958},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":132},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912510977,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74s99oSK4HUZefxT3zr","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01XvdsgtSLHo33iTGTeiBc83","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\"\n\"California\"\n\"New York\"\n\"Pennsylvania\"\n\"Minnesota\"\n\"Illinois\"\n\"Virginia\"\n\"Wisconsin\"\n\"Michigan\"\n\"Massachusetts\"\n\"Florida\"\n\"Georgia\"\n\"Ohio\"\n\"Texas\"\n\"Missouri\"\n\"North Carolina\"\n\"Iowa\"\n\"Kentucky\"\n\"Indiana\"\n\"Colorado\"\n\"Washington\"\n\"Maryland\"\n\"Connecticut\"\n\"Kansas\"\n\"Oregon\"\n\"Alabama\"\n\"Oklahoma\"\n\"Arizona\"\n\"Tennessee\"\n\"South Carolina\"\n\"New Jersey\"\n\"Montana\"\n\"Arkansas\"\n\"Louisiana\"\n\"Vermont\"\n\"Alaska\"\n\"Idaho\"\n\"West Virginia\"\n\"Wyoming\"\n\"Nebraska\"\n\"District Of Columbia\"\n\"New Hampshire\"\n\"Mississippi\"\n\"Delaware\"\n\"Maine\"\n\"New Mexico\"\n\"Rhode Island\"\n\"Utah\"\n\"Nevada\"\n\"North Dakota\"\n\"South Dakota\"\n\"Hawaii\"\n\"Puerto Rico\"\n\"Virgin Islands\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912515398},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see the data includes:\n- 50 states + District of Columbia\n- Puerto Rico\n- Virgin Islands\n\nThe question asks for \"total farmers markets (excl. territories)\", so I need to exclude Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands, but include District of Columbia (it's typically treated as a state-equivalent for such statistics).\n\nNow let me create a metric that:\n1. Sums farmers_markets for all entries EXCEPT Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands\n2. Divides by the 2025 U.S. population \n3. Multiplies by 100,000\n\nI'll create a build script that does this cross-dataset calculation.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01V7aPYfe67JcodTfgYbh5Lm","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Calculate total farmers markets excluding territories\n# Exclude Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands\nfm_total = (\n    fm.filter(~fm.state_name.isin([\"Puerto Rico\", \"Virgin Islands\"]))\n    .aggregate(total_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Get 2025 US population\nus_pop = (\n    census.filter(census.NAME == \"United States\")\n    .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and calculate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fm_total.join(us_pop, fm_total.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(\n        markets_per_100k=fm_total.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000\n    )\n    .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":755,"cacheRead":17689,"cacheWrite":508,"totalTokens":18965,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.003775,"cacheRead":0.0017689000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.000635,"total":0.0061919},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":149},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912515398,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74sSKvMLKqgss1XKvf9","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01V7aPYfe67JcodTfgYbh5Lm","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1407 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912522972},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build and add this derived metric to the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_0154hDTrHagFzTLfaUPvt7Kf","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-57-dzuxeirc && xorq build .xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp_metric.txt && cat /tmp/bp_metric.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":145,"cacheRead":18197,"cacheWrite":798,"totalTokens":19153,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"o